Someone suggested being able to wield one weapon in each hand (eg: sword and 
dirk).  AD&D had a buckler which bettered your armor by 1 and allowed you
to wield two weapons.  There are also things like spiked shields which turn
the shield into a weapon.

So how about implementing these things:
	right/left handedness &ambidextrousness
	bucklers
	two weapons wielded

As someone pointed out a while ago, a pick-axe is a two handed tool.  So why
can you a)pply it while wearing a shield?  You can't w)ield any other two
handed weapon while wearing a shield.

How about keeping track of which way you are facing.  Then you cannot see
behind you, so your armor class is worse there (lose dex adjustment, shield
factor, etc.)  unless you have telepathy or the detect monster (?) intrinsic
(the one floating eyes give out) and are blind.

And I like the suggestion for a [n/y] prompt when about to walk into a pool
or a found trap.  Turn them off for traps which cannot harm you (pits when
levitating, pools when wearing identified water walking boots).  Add a 
trap_ignore option to ignore others (sleep gas when you know you are
resistant to sleep).

Add the pickup=[$!%()["?/= a]? option.

